@@ -33,13 +33,13 @@ Widget --> Cubit --> domain service --> Repository --> ObjectBox store
 - Cubits call services and repositories and hold no business rule; validation a form needs (a parseable target, two different accounts, an amount above zero) is state derived in the cubit. Widgets under a page never call a repository or a service (the pure `static` helpers aside: `CategoryService.stringToColor`...).
 - Multi-entity writes run inside `UnitOfWork.run`, which wraps `store.runInTransaction`: the callback is synchronous, so services call only synchronous repository methods inside it, and an exception aborts every write. A nested `run` joins the outer transaction. `EntryService` create, update and delete are atomic ([entries](domain/entries.md) ENTRY-005); they write only the entry and the category usages. `AccountService.deleteAccount` is one transaction too: it clears the account from entries, SMS templates and pending entries, removes its transactions and transfers and the account, and resets the default account setting ([accounts](domain/accounts.md) ACCT-004).
 - Lists are grouped once, in the cubit: `groupEntries` / `groupOperations` turn entries into `PeriodGroup`s (period, then category, totals included) in one pass, resolving each entry's category through `entry.category.targetId` against one `CategoryRepository.byId()` read per refresh (never `entry.category.target`, which is a store lookup per entry; an unattached `ToOne` throws on `targetId`, so tests attach with `makeEntry(store:)`). Widgets render the typed groups and never regroup. Range limits go into the query (`EntryQuery.from/to`), so a screen reads only what it shows; group overview's earliest date and either-or flag are separate cheap probes.
-- Nothing is stored that can be computed. Budget periods and spent come from `BudgetRevision` rows plus the category's entries (`BudgetService.summaries` / `watchSummaries`, `BudgetCalculator`); an account's balance is `openingBalanceMinor` plus the sums of its operations (`AccountService.balanceOf` / `watchBalance`, `AccountRepository.sums`); the earliest entry and operation dates are `min(dateTime)` queries. Reads never write (BUDGET-008). See [budgets](domain/budgets.md) and [accounts](domain/accounts.md).
+- Nothing is stored that can be computed. Budget periods and spent come from `BudgetRevision` rows plus the category's entries (`BudgetService.summaries` / `watchSummaries`, `BudgetCalculator`); an account's balance is `openingBalanceMinor` plus the sums of its operations (`AccountService.balanceOf` / `watchBalance`, `AccountRepository.sums`), where a halved entry counts `Entry.countedMinor`, half its amount, in both the balance and the budget spent ([entries](domain/entries.md) ENTRY-008); the earliest entry and operation dates are `min(dateTime)` queries. Reads never write (BUDGET-008). See [budgets](domain/budgets.md) and [accounts](domain/accounts.md).
 - Money is `Money`, formatted only at display ([money](domain/money.md)).
 - Time comes from an injected `Clock`, never `DateTime.now()`; see [conventions](conventions.md).
 
 ## Export and import
 
-`lib/db/transfer/` moves all data between installs as one JSON file ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md)). `transfer_format.dart` is pure Dart: versioned DTOs (`TransferDocument`) with file-local ids, strict `fromJson` validation that throws `TransferFormatException`, and `formatVersion` (4; a newer file is rejected, a version 1 file reads as having no `smsTemplates` or `categoryRules`, and a missing rule `mode` or template `currencyRegex` reads as `contains` or empty). `DataExporter` reads the repositories in one transaction and numbers each kind 1..n, so exporting an imported store gives the same file. `DataImporter` validates, then in one `UnitOfWork.run` removes every row and writes the file's, mapping file ids to new store ids; it also replaces the SMS templates and category rules and removes the pending SMS entries, keeping `Settings.lastSmsScanAt` ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md) XFER-006); it stores only facts and recomputes the rest (`isBudgetTracked` from the budgets, `Account.isDefault` from the file's `settings.defaultAccountId`, balances and budget periods on read), sets the one settings row to the file's currency, theme and default periods and stamps `schemaVersion`. `DataTransferService.importDocument` is the only import entry point: it takes the backup first and a failed backup (`BackupFailedException`) imports nothing.
+`lib/db/transfer/` moves all data between installs as one JSON file ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md)). `transfer_format.dart` is pure Dart: versioned DTOs (`TransferDocument`) with file-local ids, strict `fromJson` validation that throws `TransferFormatException`, and `formatVersion` (5; a newer file is rejected, a version 1 file reads as having no `smsTemplates` or `categoryRules`, and a missing rule `mode`, template `currencyRegex` or entry `isHalved` reads as `contains`, empty or false). `DataExporter` reads the repositories in one transaction and numbers each kind 1..n, so exporting an imported store gives the same file. `DataImporter` validates, then in one `UnitOfWork.run` removes every row and writes the file's, mapping file ids to new store ids; it also replaces the SMS templates and category rules and removes the pending SMS entries, keeping `Settings.lastSmsScanAt` ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md) XFER-006); it stores only facts and recomputes the rest (`isBudgetTracked` from the budgets, `Account.isDefault` from the file's `settings.defaultAccountId`, balances and budget periods on read), sets the one settings row to the file's currency, theme and default periods and stamps `schemaVersion`. `DataTransferService.importDocument` is the only import entry point: it takes the backup first and a failed backup (`BackupFailedException`) imports nothing.
 
 - **Backup of the open store.** ObjectBox's backup API is server-only and closing the store would invalidate every repository and cubit, so `backupOpenStore` (`migrations/backup.dart`) copies `data.mdb` inside a read transaction: the file is copy-on-write, so while a reader is open no writer reuses its snapshot's pages and the copy is one committed state. Same temporary-name-then-rename rule as the migration backup; the name is `data.mdb.pre-import-<UTC yyyyMMdd-HHmmss-SSS>`.
 - **No restart after an import.** The store stays open, so repositories and services stay valid; every screen follows the replaced rows through its `watch` streams and `SettingsCubit` through `watchChanges`. The one thing a screen can keep is a filter that names a removed id.
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ Banking SMS are read on demand from the Android inbox and become entries only wh
 - **Pending entries** are rows with a status (pending, confirmed, dismissed) and an indexed `smsKey`; the key is kept after confirm or dismiss so a message is never imported twice. `EntryFormCubit.fromPending` pre-fills the entry form from one; submitting calls `SmsImportService.confirm`, which creates the entry through `EntryService` and marks the row confirmed, in the same transaction. Swipe-dismiss and confirm all go through the service as well. A pending entry in another currency than the app's is skipped by confirm all and marked on the list and the form. `PendingEntriesCubit` also flags a "possible duplicate" per item (an entry with the same absolute amount within a day of the SMS time, `EntryRepository.existsWithAmountBetween`): a UI hint only, it blocks nothing.
 - **Unrecognized SMS.** `UnrecognizedSms` rows (unique `smsKey`, a `dismissed` flag) keep the messages that no enabled template reads but `looksLikeTransaction` (pure, in the parser) accepts; `scan` stores them in the same transaction as the pending entries, once per key, and a message is never both (a kept one a template now reads becomes pending and its row goes). `retryUnrecognized(digits:)` re-reads the non-dismissed ones with the enabled templates and turns the ones read into pending entries through the same construction as `scan`; `SmsTemplateFormCubit.submit` calls it after saving (enabling happens in that form too). `UnrecognizedSmsCubit` lists them (swipe = `dismissUnrecognized`) and "Create template" opens the template form with the message as the test sample (`initialSample`). `SmsRepository.isKnown` is about pending entries only, so a kept message can still become pending ([SMS import](domain/sms-import.md) SMS-008).
 - **Scan point.** `Settings.lastSmsScanAt` is the latest message time seen; null means never scanned, and the pending-entries cubit then asks the page for a start point (`ScanStartDialog`) instead of scanning the whole inbox. The stored point only moves forward, so a scan from an earlier point is safe.
-- **Export scope.** Templates and category rules are exported (format version 4); pending entries, unrecognized SMS and the scan point are not, and an import removes pending entries and unrecognized SMS and keeps the scan point ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md) XFER-006).
+- **Export scope.** Templates and category rules are exported (format version 4), and so is each entry's `isHalved` flag with its whole amount (format version 5); pending entries, unrecognized SMS and the scan point are not, and an import removes pending entries and unrecognized SMS and keeps the scan point ([data transfer](domain/data-transfer.md) XFER-006).
 - **UI.** `routes/pages/sms/` (pending entries, templates with a live parse preview, category rules) and `routes/popups/sms/` (scan start, new rule); the drawer tile shows only when `SmsSource.isSupported`, and so does the optional Home button (`Settings.smsImportOnHome`). Opening the pending-entries screen scans from the last scan point at once (the first ever scan asks for a start point); the sync button scans again.
 
