    `EntryService` runs each of these in one `UnitOfWork`; deleting also decrements the category usages (never below 0), and an edit that changes the category moves one usage from the old category to the new one. Budget spent and account balances are derived on read, so no write maintains them.
 6. **ENTRY-006** Inside a period group, sorting by amount lists income categories before expense categories, each side ordered by the absolute value of the category total: largest first for "amount, descending" (the default), smallest first for "amount, ascending". "Recent" keeps categories in the order of their newest entry.
 7. **ENTRY-007** A period group and each of its categories expose their income sum and their expense sum separately; income plus expense equals the signed total (ENTRY-001).
+8. **ENTRY-008** An entry has a stored `isHalved` flag (default false). A halved entry counts at half its amount, `amountMinor ~/ 2` (truncated toward zero, whichever the sign, each entry on its own), in account balances (ACCT-001) and budget spent (BUDGET-002) and nowhere else: its stored amount stays whole, and lists and totals of entries show the whole amount.
